// Pull request author: swachchhanda000
// Change: new rule
// Title: File Deletion via Find and Shred
// Sigma ID: a3c5e7f1-9b2d-4e8a-c6d7-5f3e1a2b4c0d
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-08-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1070.004
// Description: Detects the find command executing shred via the -exec flag to perform bulk secure deletion of
//   files. Unlike plain rm, shred overwrites file contents before unlinking, making recovery
//   significantly harder. Attackers use this combination to wipe forensic artifacts such as logs,
//   credentials, and shell history across entire directory trees in a single command.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/shred.1.html
//   - https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/759cff11d5b44124c5728663cebb8ed671c1c12c1ce7204fa29d852408b147c7/content
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/d826f6d9370fc59d350588c5c605409fe3c431aa/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_find_exec_shred.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/find" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-exec" and ProcessCommandLine contains "shred")
